    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.LaunchTitle">Launch several accounts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.LaunchBody">Choose your accounts and destination. SessionDock launches them in order and creates the diagonal, clickable Roblox window cascade automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.RunTitle">Run a complete template</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.RunBody">A template launches its accounts and restores scalable window positions. Assigned macros wait for Play, then loop continuously until you select Stop.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.RecordTitle">Record only what you intend</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.RecordBody">Choose Individual client or Whole session before recording; that type is saved with the macro. Do not type passwords or private messages while recording.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.SaveTitle">Save the working arrangement</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.SaveBody">Capture attributed clients and realized positions, then choose the typed macro mode and any per-client assignments in the template editor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.SettingsTitle">Focused settings cards</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.SettingsBody">Settings contains a separately launchable Advanced tour for window layout, macro safety, templates, current-batch assignments, the controller, and rarely used tools.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.Replay">Replay Get Started tour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.GetStartedAction">Start Get Started tour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.GetStartedActionHelp">Walk through accounts, named destinations, launching, recording, templates, and Settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedAction">Start Advanced tour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedActionHelp">Explore window layout, macro safety, templates, current-batch assignments, the controller, and advanced tools.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AccountAddTitle">Add an isolated account</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AccountAddBody">Add opens a separate local browser profile. Sign in only on the official Roblox page, then verify the account before returning to Home.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationDetailsTitle">Describe the destination</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationDetailsBody">Enter a required, unique name that will make this launch target easy to recognize later.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationTargetTitle">Enter the Roblox target</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationTargetBody">Enter a supported Roblox link, place ID, private-server target, tracked server, or user target.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationAccountsTitle">Choose the accounts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationAccountsBody">Select every account that should use this target. An account can belong to only one named destination; assigning it here moves its previous named assignment.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationAssignTitle">Save account assignments</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.DestinationAssignBody">Each account can have one named destination. Saving replaces its previous named assignment; a template slot can still override the destination for that run.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedLayoutTitle">Tune window layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedLayoutBody">Set cascade reveal spacing, minimum client size, the preferred monitor, and monitor-relative DPI-aware scaling for saved layouts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedMacrosTitle">Record and manage macros</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedMacrosBody">A macro permanently keeps its Individual client or Whole session type. Every playback loops until Stop. End recording with F8 or a custom global key; focus guards protect playback, which is capped at 2x.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedTemplatesTitle">Build complete templates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedTemplatesBody">Choose per-client destinations and macros, or keep a whole-session macro separate. Layout, launch, and macro choices restore together; assigned macros loop after Play until Stop.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedAssignmentsTitle">Assign the current batch</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedAssignmentsBody">Available after a macro-enabled batch launches. Select a client macro, then focus one verified Roblox client from that batch. Assigning it does not start playback; Play loops all assignments until Stop.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedControllerTitle">Control the macro loop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedControllerBody">Available after a macro-enabled batch launches. Play starts a continuous loop and becomes Stop while it runs. Closing the controller also stops it. Physical input or focus loss pauses playback until verified focus and input conditions recover. Choose 0.25x through 2x.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedTransferTitle">Transfer selected data</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedTransferBody">Export selected templates, macros, public destinations, and launch presets in a portable package, or use legacy metadata. Sign-ins and private data stay local; review keyboard-input macros before export or import.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.Preview">Guided preview — highlighted controls are not active. Use Next to move between features.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedWorkspaceTitle">Open advanced tools</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tutorial.AdvancedWorkspaceBody">Rarely needed diagnostics, integrations, and other maintenance controls remain in the Advanced workspace.</sys:String>

